<!--
================================================================================
  SEPA Credit Transfer Initiation - pain.001.001.13
  Multi-batch payroll + supplier example
================================================================================

  ISO 20022 message:   pain.001.001.13
  EPC scheme:          SEPA Credit Transfer (SCT) Customer-to-PSP
  Intent:              one debtor (a Berlin GmbH) initiates a single file
                       containing TWO Payment Information batches:
                         PmtInf #1 — monthly payroll (3 transactions:
                                     employees in DE, NL, FR)
                         PmtInf #2 — supplier payments (2 transactions:
                                     suppliers in DE and NL)
                       Five transactions total, EUR 7,892.34 control sum.

                       Exercises:
                         - Multiple PmtInf blocks in one message.
                         - Cross-border SEPA (intra-EUR-zone DE/NL/FR).
                         - Mix of unstructured remittance (employee salaries)
                           and ISO 11649 structured creditor reference
                           (supplier invoice).
                         - Two PmtInf-level execution dates (payroll on the
                           25th, suppliers on month-end).
                         - One employee with a longer compound name to
                           exercise field-width behaviour in the UI.
                         - Mix of CtgyPurp codes (SALA, SUPP) so a future
                           summary view can distinguish the two batches.

  >>>  TEST DATA - DO NOT USE FOR REAL PAYMENTS  <<<

  Every IBAN, BIC, name, address, and identifier in this file is a synthetic
  PLACEHOLDER. See tests/example-xml/README.md for the placeholder convention.

  All IBANs are checksum-valid (mod-97 = 1) but use fake bank codes:
    Debtor          : DE28500202000123456789   (DE company, Berlin)
    Employee DE     : DE95370400440111222333   (Berlin)
    Employee NL     : NL13TEST0123456789       (Amsterdam)
    Employee FR     : FR1420041010050500013M02606  (Paris)
    Supplier DE     : DE54200505500987654321   (Hamburg)
    Supplier NL     : NL61PLAC9876543210       (Rotterdam)

  BICs follow the placeholder pattern <CODE>DEFFXXX / <CODE>NLBBXXX / etc.
  Names are prefixed with "PLACEHOLDER".

  This file is structured to match the official pain.001.001.13.xsd
  published at https://www.iso20022.org. Final XSD validation lands in
  Phase 4 (per plan/04-signing-and-encryption.md is unrelated; XSD
  validation is plan/00 §3.2 — Xerces-C++ arrives with the validation UI).
================================================================================
-->
<Document xmlns="urn:iso:std:iso:20022:tech:xsd:pain.001.001.13"
          xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
    <CstmrCdtTrfInitn>

        <!-- ============================================================ -->
